# Auto-merge conflict avoidance for the branch -> main workflow
# (.github/workflows/auto-merge-claude.yml).
#
# The built-in `union` merge driver keeps BOTH sides' added lines instead of
# emitting conflict markers -- correct ONLY for append-only logs where concurrent
# sessions each add dated entries at the tail.
#
# Post-cutover note (2026-06-06, Operating_Protocols.md §15): the append-only
# logs that previously used union (Decision_Log.md + the Decision_Log/Archived_*
# archives) were retired to BigQuery (events.decision_log etc.), so NO tracked
# .md file currently needs a union driver -- the prior per-file entries pointed at
# files that no longer exist and have been removed.
#
# Do NOT add `merge=union` for the remaining live .md files: they are spec /
# working files edited IN PLACE (Watchlist.md, Strategy.md, Experiment_Parameters.md,
# Daily.md, the Weekly_*/Monthly_*/Quarterly_* cadence outputs). Union would
# duplicate edited or whole-file content; genuine concurrent edits to those are
# REAL conflicts, which the workflow correctly routes to a PR.
#
# If a NEW append-only log file is ever added, register it here, e.g.:
#   New_Append_Only_Log.md   merge=union
